Intermediate Bus Converters (IBCs) are highly efficient, isolated DC-DC modules designed to convert high-voltage (often 48V/54V) power down to an intermediate voltage (typically 8V–14V) in distributed power systems. Used in data centers and telecom, they act as the first stage to supply point-of-load (POL) converters, reducing input current to improve efficiency.

